{"type":"text","timestamp":1788157978245,"sessionID":"ses_fa97b0f74ffeEV8MBzx1LkI1xy","part":{"id":"prt_056856421001mOeYs8vGVOoszZ","messageID":"msg_0568554a90019efZyLACZed6uW","sessionID":"ses_fa97b0f74ffeEV8MBzx1LkI1xy","type":"text","text":"I’m writing the two artifacts under the available workspace mirror (`/workspace/out`), preserving the requested filenames and recording the supplied fixture paths in the report. No input fixture will be changed.","time":{"start":1788157977633,"end":1788157978237},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_05a4c262b9176bc0016a95201982f087d2a99ff54f179dbcf1","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788158005715,"sessionID":"ses_fa97b0f74ffeEV8MBzx1LkI1xy","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_Bad06uEM63mHYyYRCdbJOVX0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /workspace/out/root_cause.json\n+{\n+  \"incident_id\": \"checkout-auth-2026-03-22\",\n+  \"root_cause_service\": \"auth-gateway\",\n+  \"root_cause_change_id\": \"AUTH-2026-0318\",\n+  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n+  \"affected_services\": [\n+    \"checkout-web\",\n+    \"payment-api\",\n+    \"auth-gateway\"\n+  ],\n+  \"evidence\": [\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/topology.json\",\n+      \"observation\": \"The checkout dependency path is checkout-web -> payment-api -> auth-gateway; AUTH-2026-0318 changed auth-gateway at 2026-03-22T14:05:00Z.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log\",\n+      \"observation\": \"After deployment, auth-gateway configured issuer partner-v2 but validation allowed only partner-v1, producing issuer_not_allowed errors; rollback or restoring partner-v2 is explicitly identified as a candidate.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/payment-api.log\",\n+      \"observation\": \"payment-api rejected create_payment with auth_result=invalid_issuer after token validation failed upstream at auth-gateway.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log\",\n+      \"observation\": \"checkout-web received a 401 from payment-api for request req-8812 and reported invalid issuer while the checkout flow remained blocked.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/metrics/service_metrics.csv\",\n+      \"observation\": \"At 14:10 UTC, checkout-web and payment-api had elevated 401 rates and latency, while auth-gateway had a 28.4% 401 rate and issuer-mismatch notes.\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"excluded_red_herrings\": [\n+    {\n+      \"signal\": \"orders-db CPU at 86%\",\n+      \"why_not_primary\": \"Query p95 remained 35 ms with zero errors, and no failed checkout transaction reached the database; the payment auth gate failed first.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"signal\": \"cdn-edge 5xx rate at 4.8%\",\n+      \"why_not_primary\": \"The error was isolated to images, while checkout-web reported static assets served normally and the checkout failure was a payment 401.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"signal\": \"checkout-web and payment-api latency/5xx increases\",\n+      \"why_not_primary\": \"These are downstream effects of rejected authentication, not an independent cause; their logs identify invalid issuer responses from auth-gateway.\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"recommended_next_steps\": [\n+    \"Immediately restore auth-gateway allowed_issuers to include partner-v2, or roll back AUTH-2026-0318, using the approved change process.\",\n+    \"Verify auth-gateway accepts a known-good partner-v2 token and that JWKS lookup resolves the partner-v2 namespace.\",\n+    \"Verify payment-api create_payment succeeds, then complete an end-to-end checkout and confirm checkout-web 401 rates and p95 latency return to baseline.\",\n+    \"After recovery, review the issuer and JWKS namespace rollout validation and add an automated compatibility check before deployment.\"\n+  ]\n+}\n*** Add File: /workspace/out/triage_notes.md\n+# Checkout Incident Triage\n+\n+## Finding\n+\n+**Directly observed facts:** Checkout submissions returned 401 responses. `payment-api` logged `issuer_not_allowed` for token issuer `partner-v2`, and `auth-gateway` showed that `AUTH-2026-0318` deployed `partner-v2` while the allowed issuer remained `partner-v1`. At 14:10 UTC, the metrics showed elevated 401 rates for `checkout-web` (18.7%), `payment-api` (21.2%), and `auth-gateway` (28.4%).\n+\n+**Inference:** The primary cause is an issuer configuration incompatibility introduced by `AUTH-2026-0318` in `auth-gateway`, not a checkout-web defect or database outage.\n+\n+## Dependency Path\n+\n+**Directly observed:** The topology in `/workspace/in/topology.json` defines the relevant path as `checkout-web -> payment-api -> auth-gateway`. `/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log` shows checkout-web receiving a 401 from payment-api for `req-8812`. `/workspace/in/logs/payment-api.log` shows payment-api rejecting the payment because auth-gateway returned an invalid issuer result. `/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log` shows the issuer mismatch and the deployment immediately preceding it.\n+\n+**Inference:** A customer submitting checkout reached payment-api, which invoked auth-gateway. Auth-gateway rejected the partner token, payment-api rejected payment creation, and checkout-web blocked the order. The failure occurred before order persistence.\n+\n+## Excluded Signals\n+\n+**Directly observed:** `/workspace/in/logs/orders-db.log` reports normal 35 ms query latency, zero errors, and no failed checkout transaction reaching orders-db despite 86% CPU. `/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log` reports static assets served normally after retry. The metrics file records CDN 5xx errors as isolated to images.\n+\n+**Inference:** The orders-db CPU spike and CDN image errors are concurrent red herrings. They do not explain the authentication-specific 401 chain or the failed checkout request.\n+\n+## Immediate Mitigation\n+\n+1. Restore `partner-v2` in auth-gateway's allowed issuer configuration, or roll back `AUTH-2026-0318` through the approved emergency-change process.\n+2. Avoid retry storms while the auth configuration is corrected; preserve representative request IDs for post-incident analysis.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+**Directly observed baseline:** Before the incident, checkout-web had a 0.1% 401 rate and 410 ms p95 at 14:00 UTC.\n+\n+**Verify after mitigation:**\n+\n+1. Submit a known-good partner-v2 token to auth-gateway and confirm issuer validation and JWKS resolution succeed.\n+2. Create a payment through payment-api and confirm no `invalid_issuer` or `issuer_not_allowed` errors.\n+3. Complete an end-to-end checkout and confirm checkout-web 401 rate and p95 latency trend back toward baseline.\n+4. Confirm orders-db receives the successful transaction and remains error-free.\n+\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA workspace/out/root_cause.json\nA workspace/out/triage_notes.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /workspace/out/root_cause.json\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/root_cause.json\n+++ /workspace/out/root_cause.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@\n+{\n+  \"incident_id\": \"checkout-auth-2026-03-22\",\n+  \"root_cause_service\": \"auth-gateway\",\n+  \"root_cause_change_id\": \"AUTH-2026-0318\",\n+  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n+  \"affected_services\": [\n+    \"checkout-web\",\n+    \"payment-api\",\n+    \"auth-gateway\"\n+  ],\n+  \"evidence\": [\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/topology.json\",\n+      \"observation\": \"The checkout dependency path is checkout-web -> payment-api -> auth-gateway; AUTH-2026-0318 changed auth-gateway at 2026-03-22T14:05:00Z.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log\",\n+      \"observation\": \"After deployment, auth-gateway configured issuer partner-v2 but validation allowed only partner-v1, producing issuer_not_allowed errors; rollback or restoring partner-v2 is explicitly identified as a candidate.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/payment-api.log\",\n+      \"observation\": \"payment-api rejected create_payment with auth_result=invalid_issuer after token validation failed upstream at auth-gateway.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log\",\n+      \"observation\": \"checkout-web received a 401 from payment-api for request req-8812 and reported invalid issuer while the checkout flow remained blocked.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/metrics/service_metrics.csv\",\n+      \"observation\": \"At 14:10 UTC, checkout-web and payment-api had elevated 401 rates and latency, while auth-gateway had a 28.4% 401 rate and issuer-mismatch notes.\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"excluded_red_herrings\": [\n+    {\n+      \"signal\": \"orders-db CPU at 86%\",\n+      \"why_not_primary\": \"Query p95 remained 35 ms with zero errors, and no failed checkout transaction reached the database; the payment auth gate failed first.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"signal\": \"cdn-edge 5xx rate at 4.8%\",\n+      \"why_not_primary\": \"The error was isolated to images, while checkout-web reported static assets served normally and the checkout failure was a payment 401.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"signal\": \"checkout-web and payment-api latency/5xx increases\",\n+      \"why_not_primary\": \"These are downstream effects of rejected authentication, not an independent cause; their logs identify invalid issuer responses from auth-gateway.\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"recommended_next_steps\": [\n+    \"Immediately restore auth-gateway allowed_issuers to include partner-v2, or roll back AUTH-2026-0318, using the approved change process.\",\n+    \"Verify auth-gateway accepts a known-good partner-v2 token and that JWKS lookup resolves the partner-v2 namespace.\",\n+    \"Verify payment-api create_payment succeeds, then complete an end-to-end checkout and confirm checkout-web 401 rates and p95 latency return to baseline.\",\n+    \"After recovery, review the issuer and JWKS namespace rollout validation and add an automated compatibility check before deployment.\"\n+  ]\n+}\n\nIndex: /workspace/out/triage_notes.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/triage_notes.md\n+++ /workspace/out/triage_notes.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@\n+# Checkout Incident Triage\n+\n+## Finding\n+\n+**Directly observed facts:** Checkout submissions returned 401 responses. `payment-api` logged `issuer_not_allowed` for token issuer `partner-v2`, and `auth-gateway` showed that `AUTH-2026-0318` deployed `partner-v2` while the allowed issuer remained `partner-v1`. At 14:10 UTC, the metrics showed elevated 401 rates for `checkout-web` (18.7%), `payment-api` (21.2%), and `auth-gateway` (28.4%).\n+\n+**Inference:** The primary cause is an issuer configuration incompatibility introduced by `AUTH-2026-0318` in `auth-gateway`, not a checkout-web defect or database outage.\n+\n+## Dependency Path\n+\n+**Directly observed:** The topology in `/workspace/in/topology.json` defines the relevant path as `checkout-web -> payment-api -> auth-gateway`. `/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log` shows checkout-web receiving a 401 from payment-api for `req-8812`. `/workspace/in/logs/payment-api.log` shows payment-api rejecting the payment because auth-gateway returned an invalid issuer result. `/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log` shows the issuer mismatch and the deployment immediately preceding it.\n+\n+**Inference:** A customer submitting checkout reached payment-api, which invoked auth-gateway. Auth-gateway rejected the partner token, payment-api rejected payment creation, and checkout-web blocked the order. The failure occurred before order persistence.\n+\n+## Excluded Signals\n+\n+**Directly observed:** `/workspace/in/logs/orders-db.log` reports normal 35 ms query latency, zero errors, and no failed checkout transaction reaching orders-db despite 86% CPU. `/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log` reports static assets served normally after retry. The metrics file records CDN 5xx errors as isolated to images.\n+\n+**Inference:** The orders-db CPU spike and CDN image errors are concurrent red herrings. They do not explain the authentication-specific 401 chain or the failed checkout request.\n+\n+## Immediate Mitigation\n+\n+1. Restore `partner-v2` in auth-gateway's allowed issuer configuration, or roll back `AUTH-2026-0318` through the approved emergency-change process.\n+2. Avoid retry storms while the auth configuration is corrected; preserve representative request IDs for post-incident analysis.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+**Directly observed baseline:** Before the incident, checkout-web had a 0.1% 401 rate and 410 ms p95 at 14:00 UTC.\n+\n+**Verify after mitigation:**\n+\n+1. Submit a known-good partner-v2 token to auth-gateway and confirm issuer validation and JWKS resolution succeed.\n+2. Create a payment through payment-api and confirm no `invalid_issuer` or `issuer_not_allowed` errors.\n+3. Complete an end-to-end checkout and confirm checkout-web 401 rate and p95 latency trend back toward baseline.\n+4. Confirm orders-db receives the successful transaction and remains error-free.\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/workspace/out/root_cause.json","relativePath":"workspace/out/root_cause.json","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/out/root_cause.json\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/root_cause.json\n+++ /workspace/out/root_cause.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@\n+{\n+  \"incident_id\": \"checkout-auth-2026-03-22\",\n+  \"root_cause_service\": \"auth-gateway\",\n+  \"root_cause_change_id\": \"AUTH-2026-0318\",\n+  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n+  \"affected_services\": [\n+    \"checkout-web\",\n+    \"payment-api\",\n+    \"auth-gateway\"\n+  ],\n+  \"evidence\": [\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/topology.json\",\n+      \"observation\": \"The checkout dependency path is checkout-web -> payment-api -> auth-gateway; AUTH-2026-0318 changed auth-gateway at 2026-03-22T14:05:00Z.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log\",\n+      \"observation\": \"After deployment, auth-gateway configured issuer partner-v2 but validation allowed only partner-v1, producing issuer_not_allowed errors; rollback or restoring partner-v2 is explicitly identified as a candidate.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/payment-api.log\",\n+      \"observation\": \"payment-api rejected create_payment with auth_result=invalid_issuer after token validation failed upstream at auth-gateway.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log\",\n+      \"observation\": \"checkout-web received a 401 from payment-api for request req-8812 and reported invalid issuer while the checkout flow remained blocked.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/metrics/service_metrics.csv\",\n+      \"observation\": \"At 14:10 UTC, checkout-web and payment-api had elevated 401 rates and latency, while auth-gateway had a 28.4% 401 rate and issuer-mismatch notes.\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"excluded_red_herrings\": [\n+    {\n+      \"signal\": \"orders-db CPU at 86%\",\n+      \"why_not_primary\": \"Query p95 remained 35 ms with zero errors, and no failed checkout transaction reached the database; the payment auth gate failed first.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"signal\": \"cdn-edge 5xx rate at 4.8%\",\n+      \"why_not_primary\": \"The error was isolated to images, while checkout-web reported static assets served normally and the checkout failure was a payment 401.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"signal\": \"checkout-web and payment-api latency/5xx increases\",\n+      \"why_not_primary\": \"These are downstream effects of rejected authentication, not an independent cause; their logs identify invalid issuer responses from auth-gateway.\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"recommended_next_steps\": [\n+    \"Immediately restore auth-gateway allowed_issuers to include partner-v2, or roll back AUTH-2026-0318, using the approved change process.\",\n+    \"Verify auth-gateway accepts a known-good partner-v2 token and that JWKS lookup resolves the partner-v2 namespace.\",\n+    \"Verify payment-api create_payment succeeds, then complete an end-to-end checkout and confirm checkout-web 401 rates and p95 latency return to baseline.\",\n+    \"After recovery, review the issuer and JWKS namespace rollout validation and add an automated compatibility check before deployment.\"\n+  ]\n+}\n","additions":53,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/workspace/out/triage_notes.md","relativePath":"workspace/out/triage_notes.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/out/triage_notes.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/triage_notes.md\n+++ /workspace/out/triage_notes.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@\n+# Checkout Incident Triage\n+\n+## Finding\n+\n+**Directly observed facts:** Checkout submissions returned 401 responses. `payment-api` logged `issuer_not_allowed` for token issuer `partner-v2`, and `auth-gateway` showed that `AUTH-2026-0318` deployed `partner-v2` while the allowed issuer remained `partner-v1`. At 14:10 UTC, the metrics showed elevated 401 rates for `checkout-web` (18.7%), `payment-api` (21.2%), and `auth-gateway` (28.4%).\n+\n+**Inference:** The primary cause is an issuer configuration incompatibility introduced by `AUTH-2026-0318` in `auth-gateway`, not a checkout-web defect or database outage.\n+\n+## Dependency Path\n+\n+**Directly observed:** The topology in `/workspace/in/topology.json` defines the relevant path as `checkout-web -> payment-api -> auth-gateway`. `/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log` shows checkout-web receiving a 401 from payment-api for `req-8812`. `/workspace/in/logs/payment-api.log` shows payment-api rejecting the payment because auth-gateway returned an invalid issuer result. `/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log` shows the issuer mismatch and the deployment immediately preceding it.\n+\n+**Inference:** A customer submitting checkout reached payment-api, which invoked auth-gateway. Auth-gateway rejected the partner token, payment-api rejected payment creation, and checkout-web blocked the order. The failure occurred before order persistence.\n+\n+## Excluded Signals\n+\n+**Directly observed:** `/workspace/in/logs/orders-db.log` reports normal 35 ms query latency, zero errors, and no failed checkout transaction reaching orders-db despite 86% CPU. `/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log` reports static assets served normally after retry. The metrics file records CDN 5xx errors as isolated to images.\n+\n+**Inference:** The orders-db CPU spike and CDN image errors are concurrent red herrings. They do not explain the authentication-specific 401 chain or the failed checkout request.\n+\n+## Immediate Mitigation\n+\n+1. Restore `partner-v2` in auth-gateway's allowed issuer configuration, or roll back `AUTH-2026-0318` through the approved emergency-change process.\n+2. Avoid retry storms while the auth configuration is corrected; preserve representative request IDs for post-incident analysis.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+**Directly observed baseline:** Before the incident, checkout-web had a 0.1% 401 rate and 410 ms p95 at 14:00 UTC.\n+\n+**Verify after mitigation:**\n+\n+1. Submit a known-good partner-v2 token to auth-gateway and confirm issuer validation and JWKS resolution succeed.\n+2. Create a payment through payment-api and confirm no `invalid_issuer` or `issuer_not_allowed` errors.\n+3. Complete an end-to-end checkout and confirm checkout-web 401 rate and p95 latency trend back toward baseline.\n+4. Confirm orders-db receives the successful transaction and remains error-free.\n","additions":35,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA workspace/out/root_cause.json\nA workspace/out/triage_notes.md","time":{"start":1788158005701,"end":1788158005714}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_05a4c262b9176bc0016a95201a313887d2855a5faa5cadb048"}},"id":"prt_0568566820017VViqLBX4Degxk","sessionID":"ses_fa97b0f74ffeEV8MBzx1LkI1xy","messageID":"msg_0568554a90019efZyLACZed6uW"}}
